# Generated transcriptions
out/
*.cho
*.chopro

# Evaluation: manifests, reference annotations and model estimates. The
# annotations are other people's work under their own licences, and the
# estimates are derived from audio -- neither belongs in the repo. A manifest
# names a corpus's own files, so it lives with the corpus; EVALUATION.md says
# how to build one. The whole directory goes, because it is where `manifest
# --output` writes by habit. Anchored with a leading slash: `eval/` on its own
# would also ignore src/songscribe/eval/, and a new module there would never be
# added.
/eval/
*.lab
annotations/
estimates/
.eval-cache/
# Word timelines for placement scoring hold lyric text, which hard constraint 5
# keeps out of the repo. songscribe.eval.reference refuses to write any other
# suffix, so this one rule covers them all.
*.words.json
# Corpora land here: downloaded annotation archives and their extracted trees.
# Anchored like /eval/ above, so tests/data/ and src/songscribe/data/ stay addable.
# Ignored wholesale rather than by extension, because Isophonics also ships
# .ttl, .svl and .txt alongside the .lab files.
/data/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
